cal CA and successful integration with RHEL's system trust store. The provider-wide restart protocol was also strong: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered system, artifact, key, root-trust, and issued-leaf behavior.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots did not inventory the CA-specific filesystem paths or trust contents, but direct pre- and post-restart commands observed those states and behaviors.","The retained reboot log's contents were not captured; only its presence is established."]}
